      "cited_excerpt": "The two opinion frames are stacked without a separate function, even though the reason is present.",
      "created_against_sha256": "2b4273a38fd2a44e5ebaeb57013b137cd14e3b5fc8466ecb3f3780d457051564",
      "criterion": "feedback_accuracy",
      "details": "Actual independent content review by /root/lesson_content_review_3; report SHA256 b803aef3454eeedee6da39d8ce850a131f827af633061a23b83e3d8800f95edf; original target presenting_a_view_supported. Owner acceptance does not resolve this advisory.",
      "excerpt": "The two opinion frames are stacked without a separate function, even though the reason is present.",
      "explanation": "The stacked-support option starts «Etter min mening mener komiteen ...». Its two attitude expressions have different subjects and can have different scopes: the speaker's assessment of what the committee believes, and the committee's policy position. Calling these equivalent opinion frames stacked without a separate function misses the actual reason the option fits poorly: it turns an official committee statement into a personal inference about that committee.",
      "finding_id": "codex-hedging_stance_markers-3-1",
      "key": "presenting_a_view_supported",
